    'Malavya': { title: 'Malavya Mahapurusha Yoga', text: 'Venus is in its own or exaltation sign in a kendra from your Lagna, forming Malavya Yoga. It gives physical beauty, grace, artistic genius, luxurious comforts, happy marriage, vehicles and wealth through refinement and taste. Life is sweet for you and you make it sweeter for those around you.' },
    'Shasha': { title: 'Shasha Mahapurusha Yoga', text: 'Saturn is in its own or exaltation sign in a kendra from your Lagna, forming Shasha Yoga. It gives authority over others, success in government, industry, land, labour and large organisations, and a position of command reached through discipline. You are a natural administrator whose power grows steadily with age.' },
    'Raja Yoga': { title: 'Raja Yoga', text: 'Lords of a kendra (angular house) and a trikona (trinal house) are conjoined in your chart, forming Raja Yoga, the combination for power and status. The texts say such a native rises above the station of their birth, commands respect and achieves a position of authority. The period of these planets\' dashas is when the yoga bears its fruit.' },
    'Dhana Yoga': { title: 'Dhana Yoga', text: 'Lords of the houses of wealth (2nd, 5th, 9th or 11th) are combined in your chart, forming Dhana Yoga, the combination for wealth. Money comes to you through multiple channels and accumulates in the periods of the planets involved. You have the capacity to become genuinely prosperous if you respect Lakshmi by sharing a portion of your gains.' },
    'Viparita Raja Yoga': { title: 'Viparita Raja Yoga', text: 'Lords of the difficult houses (6th, 8th, 12th) are placed in difficult houses, forming Viparita Raja Yoga, the paradoxical royal combination. Your greatest rises come from the misfortunes of others or from crises that would defeat most people. Obstacles turn into stepping stones. You thrive where others fail, and sudden unexpected gains are a feature of your life.' },
    'Neecha Bhanga Raja Yoga': { title: 'Neecha Bhanga Raja Yoga', text: 'A debilitated planet in your chart has its weakness cancelled by the strength of its dispositor, forming Neecha Bhanga Raja Yoga. What begins as a weakness in life becomes a source of extraordinary strength. The area of life governed by this planet will see early struggle followed by remarkable success, often greater than if the planet had been strong from the start.' },
    'Amala': { title: 'Amala Yoga', text: 'A natural benefic occupies the 10th house from your Lagna or Moon, forming Amala Yoga, the spotless combination. It gives a career of integrity, a reputation that remains unstained, lasting fame and prosperity earned through honourable means. People trust you with responsibility because you have never betrayed it.' },
